📝 Ansible + Docker Website Deployment Notes
📌 Project Goal

Automate deployment of a custom website on multiple servers using Ansible and simulate servers using Docker.

🧱 Architecture
Control Node → WSL (Ansible installed)
Managed Nodes → Docker containers
node1 (DEV)
node2 (PROD)
📁 Project Structure
ansible-web-deploy/
├── ansible.cfg
├── inventory/
├── group_vars/
├── host_vars/
├── roles/
└── site.yml

👉 This structure follows real-world DevOps standards

⚙️ 1. ansible.cfg
[defaults]
inventory = inventory/inventory.ini
host_key_checking = False
📖 Explanation
inventory → tells Ansible where servers are defined
host_key_checking=False → avoids SSH confirmation prompt

👉 Makes commands shorter and smoother

📡 2. Inventory (Servers)
[webservers]
node1 ansible_host=127.0.0.1 ansible_port=2222 ansible_user=root ansible_password=1234
node2 ansible_host=127.0.0.1 ansible_port=2223 ansible_user=root ansible_password=1234
📖 Explanation
Defines servers
Groups them as webservers
Provides:
IP
SSH port
username
password

👉 This is how Ansible knows where to connect

🧠 3. group_vars (Common Variables)
app_name: Arigato Web
company: Middleware Talents
📖 Explanation
Applies to all servers in webservers
Used inside templates

👉 Avoids repeating same values

🧠 4. host_vars (Per Server Config)
node1.yml
env: DEV
custom_msg: Hello from DEV server
node2.yml
env: PROD
custom_msg: Hello from PROD server
📖 Explanation
Each server gets different values
Enables environment-based deployment

👉 Same code → different output

📦 5. Role: nginx_site

👉 Role = reusable module in Ansible

📁 defaults/main.yml
nginx_root: /var/www/html
📖 Explanation
Default variable
Used in tasks
📁 tasks/main.yml
- name: Install nginx
  apt:
    name: nginx
    state: present
    update_cache: yes

- name: Deploy nginx config
  template:
    src: nginx.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/nginx/sites-available/default
  notify: Restart nginx

- name: Deploy dynamic index page
  template:
    src: index.html.j2
    dest: "{{ nginx_root }}/index.html"
  notify: Restart nginx

- name: Copy static files
  copy:
    src: site/
    dest: "{{ nginx_root }}/"

- name: Start nginx
  shell: service nginx start
📖 Explanation
Task	Purpose
Install nginx	install web server
Deploy config	apply nginx config
Deploy index	dynamic HTML page
Copy files	static files (CSS, pages)
Start nginx	run server

👉 This is the core automation logic

📁 handlers/main.yml
- name: Restart nginx
  shell: service nginx restart
📖 Explanation
Runs only when notified
Triggered when config/template changes

👉 Efficient restart mechanism

📁 templates/index.html.j2
<h1>{{ app_name }}</h1>
<p>Server: {{ inventory_hostname }}</p>
<p>Environment: {{ env }}</p>
<p>{{ custom_msg }}</p>
<p>Company: {{ company }}</p>
📖 Explanation
Uses Jinja variables
Dynamic per server

👉 Same file → different websites

📁 templates/nginx.conf.j2
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name _;

    root /var/www/html;
    index index.html;
}
📖 Explanation
Configures nginx server
Sets root directory
📁 files/site/about.html

Static HTML page.

👉 Copied directly to server.

📁 files/site/style.css

CSS styling file.

👉 Improves UI.

🚀 6. Main Playbook
- name: Deploy custom website to webservers
  hosts: webservers
  become: yes

  roles:
    - nginx_site
📖 Explanation
Runs on webservers
Uses nginx_site role
become: yes → run as root

👉 Entry point of automation

🧪 7. Commands Used
Test connection
ansible webservers -m ping
Run playbook
ansible-playbook site.yml
🌐 8. Output
http://localhost:9001 → node1 (DEV)
http://localhost:9002 → node2 (PROD)
🔁 9. Idempotency
Running playbook multiple times:
does NOT break system
only updates changes

👉 Core Ansible principle

⚠️ 10. Special Case (Docker)
service: module failed
Used:
shell: service nginx start

👉 Because Docker containers don’t use full init system

